    "id": "doc_1794904396212_gh0qn",
    "title": "ZYNTHEOR Native Architecture & Checkpoint Evidence",
    "content": "# ZYNTHEOR Native Architecture & Checkpoint Evidence\n\n## 1. Architecture target\nThe source defines a target decoder architecture of 10 layers, 8 attention heads, model width 512, and SwiGLU feed-forward width 1,472. These are design specifications, not proof of loaded model weights.\n\n## 2. Measured checkpoint evidence (2026-11-15)\nThe primary checkpoint payload inspected in this source archive contains 231,168 Float32 values. Legacy metadata declares 33,958,400 parameters, which does not match the serialized payload. The 41,527,808 parameter target is a specification; target checkpoint files in this archive are descriptors, not full tensor payloads. Native Cloud inference remains blocked until a compatible checkpoint is fetched and verified by the Cloud Runtime.\n\n## 3. Evidence and training policy\n- Knowledge retrieval is distinct from weight training.\n- New datasets require explicit human approval and provenance evidence before training.\n- Checkpoint integrity, training quality, and inference readiness are separate claims.\n- A status is reported only when supported by recorded runtime/test evidence.",
    "source": "docs/architecture_manifest.md",
    "format": "markdown",
    "collection": "Architecture",
    "tags": [
      "architecture",
      "transformer",
      "rope",
      "swiglu",
      "sovereign"
    ],
