  {
    "id": "doc_1794904396214_osjcn",
    "title": "Sovereign Token Verification & Constant-Time Security Specification",
    "content": "# Sovereign HMAC Token Verification Standard\n\n## 1. Timing-Attack Defense\nToken verification MUST utilize constant-time comparison via crypto.timingSafeEqual() to prevent side-channel timing attacks.\nUnder no circumstances may plain string equality (===) be used on HMAC signatures.\n\n## 2. Minimum Entropy & Tenant Isolation\nSecret keys must have at least 32 bytes of cryptographic entropy loaded from environment variables.\nEach token payload enforces strict tenantId validation, role hierarchy checks, and expiration limits.",
    "source": "docs/security_token_verification.md",
    "format": "markdown",
    "collection": "Security Invariants",
    "tags": [
      "security",
      "hmac",
      "timing-attack",
      "tenant-isolation",
      "sha256"
    ],
    "language": "en",
